<title>FINLAND: Finnish May EU-harmonised CPI up 0.9 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Finnish May EU-harmonised CPI up 0.9 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Finnish consumer price index harmonised to European Union standards rose 0.9 percent year-on-year in May after a 0.9 percent rise in April, Statistics Finland (SF) said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>				May 1997	April 1997     May 1996</p>
<p> Yr/Yr			+0.9 pct	 +0.9 pct	+1.4 pct</p>
<p> Mth/Mth		    +0.3 pct	 +0.3 pct	+0.4 pct</p>
<p> Index (base 1996=100)   101.2	    100.9	   102.6</p>
<p>According to SF's regular national method of calculation, Finnish consumer prices rose 1.0 percent year-on-year and 0.2 percent month-on-month in May, it said.</p>
<p>				May 1997	April 1997   May 1996</p>
<p> Yr/yr			+1.0 pct	 +1.0 pct    +0.7 pct</p>
<p> Mth/mth		    +0.2 pct	 +0.5 pct    +0.2 pct</p>
<p> Index (base 1990=100)   114.0	    113.8	   112.9</p>
<p>Six economists' average forecast for the national CPI figure was for a 1.0 percent rise year-on-year and a 0.2 percent rise month-on-month.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358 - 9 - 680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
